3. AC5a REFUND TEST — PASS (asserts NET 1500.00 and Count 5; mutation kills it)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
I opened TestComputeDashboardSync_ExcludedGroupRefundNets
(internal/handlers/whatif/sync_plan_exclusions_test.go:159-210) and confirmed
it asserts on plan.ExcludedGroups[0] — the struct the template actually
consumes — not on an intermediate:
    if g.Count != 5   -> "want 5 (all four payments plus the reversal)"
    const wantNetTotal = 1500.00 // 4*500 payments minus the 500 reversal
    if math.Abs(g.Total-wantNetTotal) > 0.005
       -> "Total = %.2f, want net %.2f (must NET the refund, never math.Abs it)"
    wantMonthly := wantNetTotal / months; tolerance 5.0
Fixture: 4x "Car Payment,-500.00" plus 1x "Car Payment Reversal,500.00", all
against one flagged amount-only def. The test also pins Count==5, so the
reversal is proven to be INSIDE the group (not silently dropped) while still
subtracting from the Total — exactly the netting semantics D-SY-e now
mandates. The worker deliberately used "Reversal" rather than "Refund"
because `refund` is an IncomeKeywords entry in
internal/services/classifier/classifier.go and would have reclassified the
row as Income, removing it from the outflow set the sync walks. I verified
that reasoning is load-bearing: Count==5 could not hold if the row had been
reclassified.

MUTATION MUT-A — revert the netting to the pre-ruling code
(`agg.Total += -t.Amount` -> `agg.Total += math.Abs(t.Amount)`):
  $ go test -overlay=<MUT-A> -count=1 -run '...RefundNets|...NameCollision' ./internal/handlers/whatif/
    --- FAIL: TestComputeDashboardSync_ExcludedGroupRefundNets (0.00s)
        sync_plan_exclusions_test.go:199: Total = 2500.00, want net 1500.00 (must NET the refund, never math.Abs it)
        sync_plan_exclusions_test.go:208: MonthlyAmount = 613.92, want ~368.85 (Total/months)
    FAIL	budget2/internal/handlers/whatif
The 2500.00 is precisely the ruling SY-2026-08-30a defect. The test dies on
it. The assertion is real evidence, not decoration. (MUT-A left the
NameCollision test passing — the two mutations are orthogonal, as they should
be.)

D-SY-e's negative-net clause, verified on RENDERED output: a group whose
refunds exceed its payments (1x -500.00 payment, 2x +500.00 reversals):
  PROBE-D ExcludedGroups = [{Name:Car Loan MonthlyAmount:-162.748643761302 Total:-500 Count:3}]
  PROBE-D rendered li: <li>Car Loan — $-163/mo (3 transactions)</li>
Negative Total/MonthlyAmount survives to the template and renders "as-is via
