4. AC5b DETERMINISM TEST — PASS (>=2 same-Name defs, 100 iterations, and my
   attempt-1 mutation M4 now KILLS it)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
TestComputeDashboardSync_ExcludedGroupsOrderSurvivesNameCollision
(sync_plan_exclusions_test.go:255-318). Read and confirmed against the
ruling's three requirements:
  (a) >=2 flagged defs SHARING a Name: yes —
      {ID:"sub-spotify", Name:"Subscription", Keywords:["SPOTIFY"], ExcludeFromPlanSync:true}
      {ID:"sub-netflix", Name:"Subscription", Keywords:["NETFLIX"], ExcludeFromPlanSync:true}
      Note the defs are declared spotify-FIRST while the correct tiebroken
      order is netflix-first, so the test cannot pass by accidentally
      inheriting declaration order.
  (b) >=100 in-process iterations: yes — `const iterations = 100`, each
      calling computeDashboardSync afresh.
  (c) the assertion is index-sensitive AND hash-based: each iteration
      compares `plan.ExcludedGroups[idx] != refGroups[idx]` element-by-element
      against iteration 0, and separately compares syncPlanHash to refHash.
      It also fatals if len(ExcludedGroups) != 2, so a collapse of the two
      same-Name groups into one would be caught rather than silently making
      the ordering assertion vacuous.

MUTATION MUT-B — delete ONLY the ID tiebreaker (`return ids[i] < ids[j]`),
keeping the Name comparison:
  --- FAIL: TestComputeDashboardSync_ExcludedGroupsOrderSurvivesNameCollision (0.00s)
      sync_plan_exclusions_test.go:310: iteration 1: ExcludedGroups order changed at index 0:
        [{Name:Subscription MonthlyAmount:12.742234332425069 Total:25.98 Count:2}
         {Name:Subscription MonthlyAmount:9.799455040871935 Total:19.98 Count:2}]
        vs
        [{Name:Subscription MonthlyAmount:9.799455040871935 Total:19.98 Count:2}
         {Name:Subscription MonthlyAmount:12.742234332425069 Total:25.98 Count:2}] (reference)
      FAIL

MUTATION MUT-C — my attempt-1 mutation M4, verbatim: delete the sort entirely.
At attempt 1 this SURVIVED (`ok budget2/internal/handlers/whatif 0.034s`),
which is what made the old determinism test vacuous. At attempt 2:
  --- FAIL: TestComputeDashboardSync_ExcludedGroupsOrderSurvivesNameCollision (0.00s)
      sync_plan_exclusions_test.go:310: iteration 1: ExcludedGroups order changed at index 0: ...
      FAIL
M4 is now KILLED, at iteration 1. Ruling SY-2026-08-30b's explicit
requirement ("attempt 2's test must kill that mutation") is satisfied by
running the very mutation that exposed the defect, not by an argument.

Implementation read (sync.go:217-235): the fix collects the excludedByID map
KEYS into `ids`, sorts that key slice by (Name, then ID), and builds
excludedGroups by walking the sorted keys. The def ID is used ONLY as the sort
key and is NOT added to syncExcludedGroup, so the hash canonicalization does
not gain a field — I confirmed the struct shape is still
{Name, MonthlyAmount, Total, Count} and syncPlan remains map-free.

