FINDINGS (backlog — none block acceptance)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
F1 (cosmetic, contract-compliant): a negative net group renders as
   "$-163/mo" (dollar sign before the minus) rather than "-$163/mo". This is
   exactly what amended D-SY-e prescribes ("renders a negative
   Total/MonthlyAmount as-is via formatNumber"), so it is NOT a defect
   against the contract — but it is the string a user would see and may be
   worth a formatting decision before SY4 renders this figure on a second
   surface.
F2 (test-strength nit, not required by AC5b): the AC5b test pins
   ExcludedGroups order against ITERATION 0 rather than against the
   absolute expected order (netflix before spotify). Its own comment states
   "a correct ID tiebreaker must always put Netflix first", but nothing
   asserts it. This does not weaken the mutation kill — MUT-B and MUT-C both
   fail at iteration 1 — because any flip within 100 iterations is caught.
   A one-line absolute-order assertion would make the test self-documenting.
F3 (deferred by design, D-SY-g): living ACTUALS still include flagged spend
   while the synced TARGET excludes it. Owned by SY4. Confirmed only in
   scope terms: no metrics/dashboard file was touched by SY1.

