SUMMARY
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
All six acceptance criteria met, each on a quoted command's output.
Both attempt-1 FAILs are closed and PROVEN closed by the mutations that
exposed them: MUT-A kills the refund test (SY-2026-08-30a), and MUT-C — my
own attempt-1 mutation M4, which previously survived — now kills the
determinism test (SY-2026-08-30b). The original nondeterminism probe went
from 2 distinct hashes / 40 runs to 1 distinct hash / 200 runs. The oracle
passes independently, byte-identical to the lead's log, against a fixture
demonstrably extended to trap the gross-abs defect.
